{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/466858-death-for-the-deathless","id":466858,"title":"Death for the Deathless","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-02T19:18:29-07:00","id":466858,"title":"Death for the Deathless","content":"So the Rite of Return is a legacy of a past age, a beacon of Raw Power that no modern magic can hope to contest. That said, is it possible for some comparable effect (an Archmastery Effect, wrath of a Firstborn, or Discipline of some hoary elder) to destroy an Arisen utterly, or otherwise remove it permanently from the game (shunted to the Lower Depths, maybe)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","user":"shkspr1048","date":". 04-05-2015, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T22:26:52-07:00","id":467011,"title":"","content":"Not that I am aware of. Arisen can be killed but that will just but them into the &quot;dead but sleeping&quot; state which makes them inactive. However an Arisen's cult can awaken them and certain things can force an Arisen to wake up. Basically think of the Arisen as Cthulhu. You can kill them but it only delays them, they will come back.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5554-psychic_monkey","name":"Psychic_Monkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T23:44:49-07:00","id":467069,"title":"","content":"If you destroy their organs, ruin their cult, and burn their body, they'll likely be stuck for the next 1461 years. Alternatively, blow up their organs and body, forcing the cult to attempt a Twice Arisen and maybe damning them to eternal service to Ammut instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T04:54:32-07:00","id":467223,"title":"","content":"In the <b>Sothis Ascends</b> SAS the Deceived are mentioned as possibly being able to wipe a Mummy out from existence, although that power is largely GM-fiat since there's no mechanics for it there or in <b>Book of the Deceived</b>. I'm sure falling into some obsidian maw in the Sahara so Ammut eats you is a good way to obliterate yourself permanently, too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T05:26:29-07:00","id":467245,"title":"","content":"It sounds like a somewhat more powerful version of the 'Unspeaking what is Known' Utterance from Lore of the Deceived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T10:59:38-07:00","id":467613,"title":"","content":"It is the Rite of Return. The Spell of Life is oWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T13:14:04-07:00","id":467826,"title":"","content":"What happens if you take their soul before obliterating all trace of them? Is it possible to rip out a mummy's soul, and if not, what makes them different from any other supernatural?<br /> <br /> Regarding Archmastery - Archmastery allows direct manipulation of Greater Templates by 7 dots and the fundamental removal of some aspects of a creature by 8 dots so could totally do it, but would be a gross violation of the Pax Arcanum if you didn't ask the Judges' permission first, and would require an Imperial casting, which is in itself no mean feat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T15:47:18-07:00","id":467921,"title":"","content":"Arisen souls are weird. They are split into five distinct elements, one for each Pillar, have been shredded and torn down by the trials of Duat, and may operate according to entirely different rules to the souls of any other creature.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would make Arisen immune to having their soul taken. The section on their Possession Immunity states that the Rite of Return has fused itself with the Arisen's flesh, leaving no room for other creatures. By the same token, I would say that the magic required to pull the Arisen from the flesh they are fused to would need to trump the Rite of Return itself. Maybe Archmastery is capable of that, I don't know Mage very well, but I don't usually give a stuff about crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T17:41:43-07:00","id":468025,"title":"","content":"Can't take an Arisen's soul because they don't have it; their Judge does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T18:01:44-07:00","id":468043,"title":"","content":"I did run a Story Arc which took several months of playing and which led to a group of vampires permanently killing a Mummy.<br /> Why did a group of vampires kill a Mummy?<br /> <br /> Well the mummy had signifangt wealth and political/social power and was making a special drink, &quot;Lucky Thirteen&quot;, which altered mortals who drank it regularly. The drink itself is a health drink with Vitamins and nutrients. This made it so Changelings and Vampires were getting less and less Vitae/Glamor for their efforts; to the point where at most a Vampire could only get 1 Vitae no matter how much they rolled.<br /> <br /> The Vampires began researching about the Founder (the mummy) of the private corporation. Once they learned who this person was they went to assainate the Founder in the middle of the night... however for them it didn't go as planned. In addition to this Political/Social juggernaut that was a Mummy, the Mummy kept a personal guard in the form of her Cult. None of the vampires died but they fled because they were quiet wounded and noticed that the Founder was healing. They did kill the Mummy however its when she seemingly resurrected herself from her death the following day is what gave them even more concern.<br /> <br /> So they began researching. This took much planning and the retrieving of special relics, side stories within the arc, which took about 7 months for them all in all for the amount of work they went through. Yet when they finally killed the mummy because of &quot;ancient relics, a ritual and incantations&quot; she died permanently. The party lost 2 out of the 5 characters due to the Mummy and her cultists. Slowly they also worked from the shadows to shut down the Factory by making the factory appear as an unsafe work enviroment that needed to be condemed while also culling the cult.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: If your going to permanently kill a mummy, make it a story arc. Mummys are powerful and nigh unkillable beings as its very tough to permanently kill them. A starting Mummy character has much power that a mid to end game supernatural character in a different book-line would have amassed over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5554-psychic_monkey","name":"Psychic_Monkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T20:10:26-07:00","id":468093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/466858-death-for-the-deathless?p=468025#post468025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't take an Arisen's soul because they don't have it; their Judge does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the True Name. Mummies have a Five-Fold soul, remember, and in true Ancient Egyptian tradition the idea of a Mummy's &quot;soul&quot; is more than the ethereal double that is usually portrayed in modern Western usages of the term. It includes real, physical components which are self-evidently present, not in Duat.<br /> <br /> Of course, that makes the idea of stealing a Mummies soul a whole lot more complicated... Taking someone's Ka is going to be a pretty complicated experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T12:39:36-07:00","id":469528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/466858-death-for-the-deathless?p=467613#post467613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is the Rite of Return. The Spell of Life is oWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted and changed. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T09:11:09-07:00","id":471327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/466858-death-for-the-deathless?p=468093#post468093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's the True Name. Mummies have a Five-Fold soul, remember, and in true Ancient Egyptian tradition the idea of a Mummy's &quot;soul&quot; is more than the ethereal double that is usually portrayed in modern Western usages of the term. It includes real, physical components which are self-evidently present, not in Duat.<br /> <br /> Of course, that makes the idea of stealing a Mummies soul a whole lot more complicated... Taking someone's Ka is going to be a pretty complicated experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their Judge owns the complete soul of the Arisen via the True Name. Someone messes with the Soul and then the Judge immediately utters his Mummy's True Name and it is immediately yanked back to Duat and sent to put you down for having that much hubris. Never mind that the Arisen don't have their complete 5 Part Soul, as much of it was stripped away in the trials that were a result of the Rite of Return. That's why they have to have dots of pillars, and don't have 5 dots in all pillars... 'cause they have to piece it back together. Who has the complete picture? The Judge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","user":"DesolateDolly","date":". 04-07-2015, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T14:10:32-07:00","id":471672,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's anything that says the Judges <i>keep</i> the bits of soul broken away during the trials. In fact, since the harrowing of the soul occurs as the Arisen is passed from Judge to Judge, it would be easy to assume that if the pieces are kept, they're kept by different Judges. The final Judge is the one the Arisen pronounced their Decree to once the inviolable Pillar has been determined. And anyway, if the Judge does have the complete soul, logically that would make buying Pillar dots as worthy of forcing a Descent check as buying a dot of Memory, since it represents buying something back from the Judge.<br /> <br /> Their souls are damaged, for sure, but it's the True Name that gives the Judges their mastery of the Arisen. The soul of an Arisen is what bounces between Duat and the living world whenever they are Called, and there doesn't appear to be any indication that their Judges keep it when the Arisen is active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T03:17:45-07:00","id":472467,"title":"","content":"The complete picture I was referring to is not &quot;soul stuff&quot; or a ghost that has been divided into five pieces, or many, but rather the <i>True Name</i>. As a True Name is more than just a word, it is the perfect heavenly expression of everything you are so much that it's utterance gives the utterer absolute power over you.<br /> <br /> The separation of &quot;soul stuff&quot; was in reference to the concept that there are physical remnants of the soul in the Arisen's body that would allow, say, a mage to manipulate the Mummy's soul. The only parts left are the Pillars, the core pillars belong to the Judge that the Arisen has in their Decree, all else are gravy.<br /> <br /> Basically, killing a Mummy until the next Sothic Turn is about as good as it gets. I mean, it's the Rite of Return, anything that so simply disrupts it just because one did some research would neuter the Mummy's place in the World of Darkness. Not even the Arisen understand the Rite, and I would say that understanding the Rite is the only way you could disrupt it, and I would also remind that knowledge of the Rite was lost with Irem. So short of finding the Lost City, talking to the Shaniatu, or the Judges, the best way to &quot;kill&quot; a Mummy is to destroy his tomb, his body and his cult. Feel free to change that in your stories all you care to, but I think putting him down until Sothis ascends again is a fairly effective enough death for any antagonist in a chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T04:25:54-07:00","id":472486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/466858-death-for-the-deathless?p=472467#post472467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The complete picture I was referring to is not &quot;soul stuff&quot; or a ghost that has been divided into five pieces, or many, but rather the <i>True Name</i>. As a True Name is more than just a word, it is the perfect heavenly expression of everything you are so much that it's utterance gives the utterer absolute power over you.<br /> <br /> The separation of &quot;soul stuff&quot; was in reference to the concept that there are physical remnants of the soul in the Arisen's body that would allow, say, a mage to manipulate the Mummy's soul. The only parts left are the Pillars, the core pillars belong to the Judge that the Arisen has in their Decree, all else are gravy.<br /> <br /> Basically, killing a Mummy until the next Sothic Turn is about as good as it gets. I mean, it's the Rite of Return, anything that so simply disrupts it just because one did some research would neuter the Mummy's place in the World of Darkness. Not even the Arisen understand the Rite, and I would say that understanding the Rite is the only way you could disrupt it, and I would also remind that knowledge of the Rite was lost with Irem. So short of finding the Lost City, talking to the Shaniatu, or the Judges, the best way to &quot;kill&quot; a Mummy is to destroy his tomb, his body and his cult. Feel free to change that in your stories all you care to, but I think putting him down until Sothis ascends again is a fairly effective enough death for any antagonist in a chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Only as long as you aren't talking Rank 6+ or Arcanum 6+ entities, then we are entirely agreed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T12:27:07-07:00","id":473217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/466858-death-for-the-deathless?p=472486#post472486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Only as long as you aren't talking Rank 6+ or Arcanum 6+ entities, then we are entirely agreed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like the Shaniatu or the Judges? 'cause while Mage the Awakening might have an old 1e supplement (and indeed Mummy is still 1e) that detailed in the statistical abilities of Rank 6+ entities (entities that <i>everywhere else</i> say pointedly do not require statistics because they are <i>plot devices</i> and effectively insurmountable unless you want them to be), this is Mummy we're talking about so I'll answer from the perspective that this is a &quot;Mummy the Curse&quot; game and not a &quot;Mage the Awakening&quot; game since they are going to have different themes and quote this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can?p=423304#post423304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All of this is correct. Expanding a bit on #3, each of the game lines have an intended &quot;specialness&quot; to them in which one line does not co-opt another. It would be as inappropriate for mages to make mummies as it would be for mummies to have an utterance that awakens mortals as mages. Even more importantly, it is a key part of mummy that the Rite is something miraculous from a bygone age of epic sorcery, something that happened once and transformed the world and then has never (and could never) be duplicated without very extensive changes to the setting. Mummies are living relics (literally) of antiquity, rooted in a glorious past that has decayed until its traces barely remain. This is part of their tragedy, especially since the decline of Memory means they have personally decayed and lost their past even right along with the other legacies of Irem. They must struggle to hold onto the pieces of who they were and expend enormous effort to probe the mysteries of where they came from.<br /> <br /> This is not to say that you are having badwrong fun if you want to tell a story of modern mystics making their own mummies, only that canon has strong reasons not to permit that within official material.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a mage is not intended to create a Mummy, or to be capable of replicating the Rite of Return, I suspect that disrupting the Rite of Return would be equally suspect regardless of a Mage's Arcanum score. If we're talking about what is official material, it would seem, that you can only kill a Mummy in the ways described.<br /> <br /> If we're talking about what you want to do in your own game? Again, that's whatever you want to do. It seems now we're getting into an argument of whether or not the RAW supports it or the RAI supports it and I'll always favour the RAI in an abstract set of rules.<br /> <br /> (( The thread the quote is taken from can be found here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/422464-crossover-questions-dealing-with-mummies-and-mages-please-answer-if-you-can\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...wer-if-you-can</a> ))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T14:54:37-07:00","id":473384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> this is Mummy we're talking about </div> </div> </div>The original question was specifically bringing in First Born, Archmasters etc. If you're doing that, you're already pretty commited to ignoring thematic purity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T15:30:41-07:00","id":473431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/466858-death-for-the-deathless?p=473384#post473384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The original question was specifically bringing in First Born, Archmasters etc. If you're doing that, you're already pretty commited to ignoring thematic purity.</div> </div> </div> </div>And as Dolly pointed out, messing with the Rite of Return to create Mummies or destroy them forever seems to be strictly in the realm of 'outside normal canon'. So in that case, if you want Archmasters/First Born/Elder vampires to be able to kill Mummies, go right ahead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2984-jibkisamabi","name":"JibKisamabi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T15:48:12-07:00","id":473460,"title":"","content":"That said, Mummies have no equivalent to Archmasters/Vampire Elders. Instead, each Arisen rises with the kind of power you wouldn't expect to see outside of an endgame character. Thus, from a narrative perspective, it almost seems appropriate to rule that all Arisen are possessed of the kind of innate majesty possessed by only the most powerful of other splats, and the Rite itself was created by creatures beyond even them. Even in a crossover game, I would generally rule that messing with the greatest act of sorcery ever performed (at least in this timeline) would be well outside the scope of just about any power in the universe. Of course, at this point we are just debating personal preferences when it comes to non-canon interactions, but that one is mine.<br /> <br /> Besides, creatures with that amount of power would probably find it a whole lot simpler to just disable the Arisen until their next Sothic Turn through the aforementioned &quot;destroy body, slaughter cult&quot; method. 1,463 years of peace is close enough to a win condition that going through the added difficulty of wrestling with the Judges seems more than a little unnecessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T18:12:21-07:00","id":473568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/466858-death-for-the-deathless?p=473460#post473460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, Mummies have no equivalent to Archmasters/Vampire Elders. Instead, each Arisen rises with the kind of power you wouldn't expect to see outside of an endgame character. Thus, from a narrative perspective, it almost seems appropriate to rule that all Arisen are possessed of the kind of innate majesty possessed by only the most powerful of other splats, and the Rite itself was created by creatures beyond even them. Even in a crossover game, I would generally rule that messing with the greatest act of sorcery ever performed (at least in this timeline) would be well outside the scope of just about any power in the universe. Of course, at this point we are just debating personal preferences when it comes to non-canon interactions, but that one is mine.<br /> <br /> Besides, creatures with that amount of power would probably find it a whole lot simpler to just disable the Arisen until their next Sothic Turn through the aforementioned &quot;destroy body, slaughter cult&quot; method. 1,463 years of peace is close enough to a win condition that going through the added difficulty of wrestling with the Judges seems more than a little unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is pretty much my viewpoint, thank you for stating it so well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2984-jibkisamabi","name":"JibKisamabi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T01:36:04-07:00","id":473982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And as Dolly pointed out, messing with the Rite of Return to create Mummies or destroy them forever seems to be strictly in the realm of 'outside normal canon'. So in that case, if you want Archmasters/First Born/Elder vampires to be able to kill Mummies, go right ahead. </div> </div> </div>I know they said that. I don't know why you think it relevant to what I said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thus, from a narrative perspective, it almost seems appropriate to rule that all Arisen are possessed of the kind of innate majesty possessed by only the most powerful of other splats, and the Rite itself was created by creatures beyond even them. </div> </div> </div>I disagree. The best thing narratively would be to simply not make it a question. If you already have a great story in mind, it's irrelevant, if you don't it's still irrelevant because it's never going to come up in a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T03:15:57-07:00","id":474020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/466858-death-for-the-deathless?p=473982#post473982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know they said that. I don't know why you think it relevant to what I said.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I disagree. The best thing narratively would be to simply not make it a question. If you already have a great story in mind, it's irrelevant, if you don't it's still irrelevant because it's never going to come up in a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand you're point. You seem to have said what I said, but said it as if you're disagreeing with what I said. (That's a mouthful!)<br /> <br /> I said: If we're talking about what you want to do in your own game? Again, that's whatever you want to do. It seems now we're getting into an argument of whether or not the RAW supports it or the RAI supports it and I'll always favour the RAI in an abstract set of rules.<br /> <br /> My meaning: It's not intended for anyone to be able to undo the Rite of Return, however, if you want that to happen in your game, go ahead. It's just not a canon intention by the writers, or so it would seem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T03:29:32-07:00","id":474022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/466858-death-for-the-deathless?p=474020#post474020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My meaning: It's not intended for anyone to be able to undo the Rite of Return, however, if you want that to happen in your game, go ahead. It's just not a canon intention by the writers, or so it would seem.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not intended for anyone to be able to undo the Embrace, Awaken a sleeper intentionally, separate a Werewolf from their spirit form, or allow a Promethean to skip right to humanity. Except that Archmages and other similarly powered individuals/gods are explicitly allowed to do so with the rules that expand and detail their capabilities.<br /> <br /> Mummy is 1E, and 1E supplements apply when discussing crossovers - especially in a topic that directly asks whether Archmages could affect them. You may not like that, but it is directly written as well within the limits of their powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T04:46:43-07:00","id":474092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/466858-death-for-the-deathless?p=473982#post473982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. The best thing narratively would be to simply not make it a question. If you already have a great story in mind, it's irrelevant, if you don't it's still irrelevant because it's never going to come up in a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrug* As I said, we are just talking preferences when it comes to non-canon interactions. I was just stating my own. We're not exactly taking different sides here.<br /> <br /> Personally, from the perspective of what makes a good story, giving newer, modern magics the ability to trump the Rite of Return doesn't mesh well with Mummy's themes. One of the core ideas of the line is that magic has been lost and is not what it was in the glory days of Irem. Thus, from a narrative perspective, my own opinion is simply that Mummy's themes are not well served by living mages being able to revoke the Rite. Now, it's entirely possible that someone will come up with a story in which the removing of the Mummy template is central to telling a good story, and that they consider the benefits of such to be worth that dilution of theme. That's fine, and entirely up to them, but I have yet to concoct such a story for myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T05:14:08-07:00","id":474129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/466858-death-for-the-deathless?p=474092#post474092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrug* As I said, we are just talking preferences when it comes to non-canon interactions. I was just stating my own. We're not exactly taking different sides here.<br /> <br /> Personally, from the perspective of what makes a good story, giving newer, modern magics the ability to trump the Rite of Return doesn't mesh well with Mummy's themes. One of the core ideas of the line is that magic has been lost and is not what it was in the glory days of Irem. Thus, from a narrative perspective, my own opinion is simply that Mummy's themes are not well served by living mages being able to revoke the Rite. Now, it's entirely possible that someone will come up with a story in which the removing of the Mummy template is central to telling a good story, and that they consider the benefits of such to be worth that dilution of theme. That's fine, and entirely up to them, but I have yet to concoct such a story for myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Newer modern magics&quot; implies a fundamental misunderstanding about what Awakened magic even is... and to dismiss Archmages as just human sorcerers is to fundamentally underestimate the order of magnitude past which they exceed any other splat in the World of Darkness if they go gloves-off. Any Master Mage in 1e has the ability to single-handedly end the world if unopposed, and Archmages are the whispered legends of even them.<br /> <br /> The ability to undo the Rite of Return may go against the theme of Mummy, but the inability to break the rules goes even more against the theme of Mage, which is about consequences. Which goes back to my point earlier - the reason an Archmage would never undo the Rite of Return on a Mummy is not because they could not, but because doing so without the permission of the Judges would get them killed by any number of cosmically powerful entities for breaking the Pax. It's not about inability, it's about unwillingness. <br /> <br /> ...and if they only circumstance in which an Archmage would undo the Rite comes tied with permission from the Judges anyway, I'm not sure how that actually goes against the theme of Mummy at all.<br /> <br /> Besides which, if your characters are on speaking terms with Gods and Archmasters, the themes of Mummy you seem to most like have probably already become pretty diluted anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T10:35:52-07:00","id":474477,"title":"","content":"Imperial Mysteries was the book that brought me back to Mage. In my NWoD, they're not going to be able to meddle with the Rite of Return for the same reason why they can't meddle with the Fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:30:06-07:00","id":474846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/466858-death-for-the-deathless?p=474129#post474129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Newer modern magics&quot; implies a fundamental misunderstanding about what Awakened magic even is... and to dismiss Archmages as just human sorcerers is to fundamentally underestimate the order of magnitude past which they exceed any other splat in the World of Darkness if they go gloves-off. Any Master Mage in 1e has the ability to single-handedly end the world if unopposed, and Archmages are the whispered legends of even them.<br /> <br /> The ability to undo the Rite of Return may go against the theme of Mummy, but the inability to break the rules goes even more against the theme of Mage, which is about consequences. Which goes back to my point earlier - the reason an Archmage would never undo the Rite of Return on a Mummy is not because they could not, but because doing so without the permission of the Judges would get them killed by any number of cosmically powerful entities for breaking the Pax. It's not about inability, it's about unwillingness.<br /> <br /> ...and if they only circumstance in which an Archmage would undo the Rite comes tied with permission from the Judges anyway, I'm not sure how that actually goes against the theme of Mummy at all.<br /> <br /> Besides which, if your characters are on speaking terms with Gods and Archmasters, the themes of Mummy you seem to most like have probably already become pretty diluted anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we're actually disagreeing on anything important here. The net result is the same, in that Archmasters aren't going to be undoing the Rite. As to whether it's because they're unable or unwilling, I see no reason why you have to offer a definitive in-universe explanation if you're playing a crossover. From the perspective of a Mummy player, the reason the Archmaster isn't able to end them permanently is because no sorcery can ever match that of the Shan'iatu. If you have an Archmaster player, the reason you give them is because the Judges would annihilate them for doing such an act without permission. The net result is the same, in that the Rite will remain untouched, and there's no reason to poison either splat's themes by providing a definitive &quot;truth&quot;.<br /> <br /> And if one side is an NPC, you give the explanation most thematically appropriate to the one who actually is a player, because the feelings of an NPC are irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T14:56:29-07:00","id":474926,"title":"","content":"An archmaster probably <i>could</i> undo/counter the Rite of Return, but would need major backup to deflect the counter-offensive of the Judges. A sneakier way to go about it would be to 'encourage' the Arisen along the path of Apotheosis, and squash them at their (relative) weakest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}